    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d8ad18a9",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image features a black woman in a vintage-style dress, sitting on the floor with a skeptical, questioning expression, accompanied by text that reads 'am i gonna wish you happy birthday?' and 'dafuq else im'a do'. The overall intent is to humorously express exasperation or sarcasm about a mundane social obligation — wishing someone a happy birthday — by implying that it's the only thing one can possibly do in that context. The meme uses the woman's facial expression and posture to convey a sense of weary resignation or mock confusion. There is no toxicity present in this meme. The image and text are juxtaposed to create a relatable, comedic scenario about social expectations, not to target or demean any group. The meme is intended for lighthearted, self-deprecating humor, not to promote hate, abuse, or harmful stereotypes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d3f0ce6f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
